Package: InveRseRegex
Title: Infer Regular Expressions from Example Text
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("InveRseRegex", "Authors", email = "noreply@example.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A lightweight tool for the inverse of the usual regex workflow:
    instead of writing a pattern to find text, you provide the text and the
    value(s) you want to extract, and 'InveRseRegex' infers a regular
    expression that captures them. Patterns are generalised at a configurable
    level (from a literal escape to compact character-class quantifiers) and
    verified against the input before being returned, so they can be used
    directly with 'stringr', 'grepl()', 'regmatches()' and similar.
